    "totalDuration": "25 yrs 10 mos",
    "description": "* Engaged in full-cycle application development processes, including requirements gathering, design, implementation, unit and regression testing, documentation and product support for Ixia IxOS platform/server/clients product and its new features.\n* Worked on large scale multi-threaded C++ applications with a code base of about 8M+ lines of code.\n* Areas of development include both Server and Client applications: IxServer - a multi-threaded Windows server application; IxExplorer - a Windows GUI application, and IxTclHal - a Tcl wish console application. Development scope also extended to middleware components between layers and system components, including embedded Linux-based CPUs.\n* Key member in big projects that produced new lines of products to bring large income to the company. This involved starting from scratch to the final integration to bring up new boards that explored new technologies and improved productivity . An example is IxYukon board. It was recognized as a worldwide Product of the Year in 2009 in the 10GE Test Market.\n* Interacted with ASIC designers, FPGA engineers, transceiver/PHY suppliers, read hardware datasheets, specifications, as well as schematic documents to implement features that interact between hardware and software such as transceivers, adapters, etc.\n* Oftentimes interfaced directly with domestic and international customers.\n* Successfully mentored other developers and QA engineers with guidance, design and code review activities\n* Highly motivated team player with excellent writing and communication skills\n* Very detailed-oriented and bug-free developer\n* Earned a “Customer Delight” award for going “above and beyond” in debugging a customer problem involving a broken network configuration",
